 12.3 Delete and replace with the following: "Other System Features. The pipe sizes, hose valves, hose, water supply, and other details for new construction shall be in accordance with this standard and Chapter 33 of the New York City Building Code . Temporary risers shall be at least 4 inches in (102 mm) diameter for structures less than 450 feet high (137 m) and at least 6 inches (152 mm) in diameter for structures 450 feet (137 m) high or more. There shall be as many risers as will be, or were, required for the permanent system. Each such riser shall be connected to a cross connection that is supplied through FDC(s) at the street level and shall be equipped on each floor with a 2 1/2 inch (64 mm) hose outlet valve. The installations shall be made so that each riser, cross connection, and branch line can be plugged or capped when work is not being done on the system."

